Z||000000||baldlobo||09-21-2000||10:45 PM||||I'm wondering what would cause the front driver's side fender to snap when the door is open all the way?||||reg||5
Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||09-21-2000||11:13 PM||||Sounds like the gap between the door and fender is too tight.  The plastic panels can expand and contract in extreme temperatures narrowing the gap and causing the door to rub.<P>Check the gap to see if it's narrow towards the bottom, the poping noise might be the lower portion hitting somewhere, especially if you have the GT rocker door trim there.<P>It could also be a bad door spring or it's popping where it's mounting on the hinge, but I doubt it.<P>Try to see if it's one of these two things and post an update.  Find out if the lower fender mount is riveted in too, look under the rocker panel from under the car.  If the rivets have been replaced with bolts and nuts just loosen them and shove the fender forward to widen the gap enough and tighten again.<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">           <BR>           <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> <p>[This message has been edited by HugGRRRFiero (edited 09-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||09-21-2000||11:14 PM||||It sounds like the panels are not aligned properly. Can you see a rub mark on the fender or the door?<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||baldlobo||09-23-2000||07:52 PM||||I ask the question because the drivers side front fender is broken, just under the black molding from halfway to the inerfender to door jamb.||||reg||1
